[Event "Rook endgames: behind the passed pawn"]
[Result "1-0"]
[Variant "Standard"]
[ChapterURL "https://lichess.org/study/GhFJctMz/vZQa2yT6"]
[FEN "8/8/1k1P4/1r6/R5K1/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[SetUp "1"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/8/8/1k1P4/1r6/R5K1/8/8/8_w_-_-_0_1"]

{ Time to learn rook endings. First rule: your rook belongs behind the passed pawn. [%cal Ya4d4] }
1. Rd4 { Behind the pawn, where it belongs. Now nothing stops it. [%csl Gd4][%cal Gd6d8] } (1. d7 { The pawn runs off alone. Watch him park in front of it. } 1... Rd5 2. d8=Q+ Rxd8 { Your new queen lasted one move. Drawn. }) (1. Ra6+ { A free check, and a free rook for him. } 1... Kxa6 { The rook is gone and the pawn falls next. Lost. }) (1. Rb4 { You offer a trade and he is delighted. } 1... Rxb4+ { Now the pawn is all alone. You are lost. }) (1. Ra5 { Sideways, and your rook lands right beside his. } 1... Rxa5 { The rook is gone. You are lost. }) (1. Ra8 { Far from the pawn, and far from safe. } 1... Rb4+ 2. Kf3 Rb3+ { The checks never stop. Drawn. }) 1... Kc5 { He comes for your rook. Push the pawn anyway. [%cal Yd6d7] } 2. d7 { The rook shields the pawn from behind. [%csl Gd7] } (2. Rd1 { Also winning. Still behind the pawn, just further back. } 2... Kc6 { The pawn goes home all the same. }) (2. Rd2 { The same idea, one square along. Also winning. } 2... Kc6 { Behind the pawn is behind the pawn. Still winning. }) (2. Rd3 { Also fine. Any square behind the pawn does the job. } 2... Kc6 { The pawn walks home from here. }) (2. Rd5+ { A check, but you have given the rook away. } 2... Kxd5 3. d7 Rb8 { His rook stops the pawn. You are lost. }) (2. Rc4+ { Another check that hangs your rook. } 2... Kxc4 3. Kf3 Rd5 { The pawn falls next. You are lost. }) (2. Ra4 { The rook leaves the pawn to fend for itself. } 2... Kxd6 { And the pawn is simply eaten. Drawn. }) 2... Kxd4 { He took the rook. Now count it out. [%cal Yd7d8] } 3. d8=Q+ { A new queen with check, and his rook falls next. A rook would only draw. [%csl Gd8] } (3. Kf3 { The pawn cannot wait. } 3... Rb8 { His rook gets in front and the pawn is dead. You are lost. }) 1-0


