{ His pawn is ready to run and his king is guarding it. Your rook must stop it alone. }
1. e5 { The pawn sets off. Which square kills it dead? } 1... Re2 { Right behind it, and it cannot take another step. [%csl Ge2][%cal Ge2e5] } (1... Rd2+ { A check that only helps his king forward. } 2. Ke6 Kd8 3. Ra8+ { You are driven back and the pawn walks in. Lost. }) (1... Rh6+ { The same trouble: the check sends him where he wants to go. } 2. e6 Kf8 3. Ra8+ { You are lost. }) (1... Kf7 { You step aside and the pawn is free. } 2. e6+ Kf6 3. Rf1+ { Lost. }) (1... Ra2 { You offer a trade you cannot afford. } 2. Rxa2 { A bare king against a pawn. Lost. }) (1... Rh1 { Wandering off, and the rook is not even safe there. } 2. Rxh1 { Lost. }) 2. e6 { He pushes past your rook. Now what? } 2... Rd2+ { You cut his king off on the d column. The pawn is stuck for ever. [%csl Gd2] } (2... Rxe6+ { A free pawn! But look at what is left. } 3. Kxe6 { A bare king against a rook. You are lost. }) (2... Re1 { Behind the pawn again, but he was quicker. } 3. Ra8# { Mate. }) (2... Kf8 { The king wanders off the pawn's file. } 3. Ra8+ { And the pawn queens behind you. Lost. }) 0-1


